    "definitions": {
      "short": "a deity or the Deity",
      "usage": "God, god. See 430 .",
      "full": "H433. eloah אֱלֹהַּ 57 so Deut 32:17 ; לֶאֱלֹהַּ Dan 11:38 (see BD) suffix לֵאלֹהוֺ Hab 1:11 ; elsewhere אֱלוֺהַּ noun masculine god, God . (Samaritan id. , Aramaic אֱלָהּ , , Arabic , Sabean אלה DHM l.c .; — אֱלֹהַּ as found in Hebrew probably a singular formed by inference from plural אֱלֹהִים : compare Nes l.c .) — 1 a heathen god , late usage; כָּלאֱֿלוֺהַּ 2Chr 32:15 ; Dan 11:37 ; לאלהו כחו זוּ whose power is his god Hab 1:11 ; 2Kin 17:31 (but Qr אֱלֹהֵי ), בְּיָדוֺ אֱלוֺהַּ הביא אשר who doth bring God in his hand Job 12:6 (Ew Di RVm, etc.) 2 God, used in ancient poems Deut 32:15 , 17 ; Psa 18:32 , and on their basis an archaism in later poetry Job 3:4 + (41 t. Job), Psa 50:22 ; 114:7 ; 139:19 ; Prov 30:5 ; Isa 44:8 ; Hab 3:3 ; Neh 9:17 (citing Exod 34:6 where אֵל is used).",
      "rootNote": "rarely (shortened) אֱלֹהַּ ; probably prolonged (emphatic) from 410 ;",
